    <h2>1. Lack of Market Need</h2>
    <p>Many startups build solutions in search of a problem. If the market doesn’t have a clear need or pain point, the startup dies early. Always validate demand before building.</p>

    <h2>2. Poor Cash Flow Management</h2>
    <p>Even startups with traction run out of money because of poor budgeting. Understanding burn rate, runway, and profit margins is critical — and often ignored.</p>

    <h2>3. Weak Digital Presence</h2>
    <p>In today’s world, if your startup can’t be found online, it’s invisible. No website, poor SEO, inconsistent social media — all of these kill credibility.</p>

